
Kubernetes components architecture


Master components:
    1. Kube API server
        - Entry point for all REST commands used to control the cluster.
        - All administartive task are done by API server within the Master node.
        - Create/Delete/Update or Display in Kubernetes objects it has to go through this API server.
        - API server validates and configures API objects [port/services/replication/controller and deployment]
        - We interact with these API's using tool called kubectl
    
    2. ETCD
        - distributed key value store.
        - k8s uses etcd as database to store all cluster data.
        - some of data stored in etcd is - job scheduleing information, pods , state information 

    3. Kube schedular
        - Scheduler watches pods and assign the pods to run on specific host
        - New pod does not have specific node assigned when it is formed, by using user or a deployment controller or a replication controller
        - Scheduler chooses a suitable node for the pod 
    
    4. Control Manager
        - Runs the controllers in the background which run different tasks in k8s cluster
        - Performs cluster level functions (replication / tracking worker nodes / handling failures)

Workers components:
    1. Kubelet
        - This the main node agent, 
        - operates on each nodes and reads the container manifest, and mkae sure containers are active and in good conditions
        - It ensures pods of containers are operating
    
    2. Kube-proxy
        - Manages and tracks network rules on the host and managing connections.
        - Network connectivity to your Pod is permitted by these network rules from both inside and outside of your cluster.
    
    3. Pod
        - Collection of one or more Linux containers and is the smallest unit of k8s application
        



